```

**چرا این کد کار می‌کند:**
- `dir="rtl"` روی تگ `<html>` کل چیدمان را راست‌به‌چپ می‌کند و ویژگی‌های منطقی مثل `margin-inline-start` جهت را خودکار جابه‌جا می‌کنند.
- فونت «Estedad» با دو `preconnect` زودتر از `stylesheet` لود می‌شود تا تأخیر فونت کم شود و `display=swap` از متن نامرئی جلوگیری می‌کند.
- `clamp()` اندازهٔ تیتر را بین دو حد با نرخ واکنش‌گرا نگه می‌دارد، بدون media query.
- منوی موبایل فقط با `classList.toggle` باز و بسته می‌شود و `aria-expanded` برای صفحه‌خوان‌ها به‌روز می‌ماند.

```css
:root {
  --bg: #ffffff;
  --fg: #0f172a;
  --accent: #2563eb;
  color-scheme: light dark;
}

@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
    --bg: #0b1220;
    --fg: #e2e8f0;
    --accent: #60a5fa;
  }
}

:root[data-theme="dark"] {
  --bg: #0b1220;
  --fg: #e2e8f0;
  --accent: #60a5fa;
}

body {
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--fg);
  transition: background-color 0.3s, color 0.3s;
}
```

**Why this works:** Custom properties are inherited live values, so redefining `--bg`/`--fg` on `:root` recolors every descendant that reads them with `var()` — no selector duplication, one source of truth per theme. The OS preference is respected by default via the media query; the `:not([data-theme="light"])` guard lets a manual toggle *override* the OS setting instead of fighting it, and `data-theme="dark"` forces dark even on light-OS machines. `color-scheme: light dark` additionally tells the browser which palettes the page supports, fixing form controls, scrollbars and the canvas background in dark mode. Persist the choice in `localStorage` and set `data-theme` before first paint (inline script in `<head>`) to avoid a theme flash; three-state toggles (light/dark/auto) should just remove the attribute to fall back to the media query.

Custom properties (--name) participate in the cascade and inherit, unlike Sass variables which compile away. Redefining them on a scope (like [data-theme='light']) instantly re-themes everything that uses them, and they can change at runtime from JS.

```css
:root { --accent: #10b981; }
.btn { background: var(--accent, #333); }
```

```js
// Reading: /search?q=arion&lang=en&lang=fa
const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
console.log(params.get('q'));        // 'arion' (null if missing)
console.log(params.getAll('lang'));  // ['en', 'fa'] — repeated keys
console.log(params.has('lang'));     // true
console.log([...params.entries()]);  // iterate everything
params.forEach((value, key) => console.log(key, value));

// Writing
const p = new URLSearchParams();
p.set('page', '2');        // add or overwrite
p.append('tag', 'js');     // append allows duplicates
p.append('tag', 'css');
console.log(p.toString()); // page=2&tag=js&tag=css
console.log(`/products?${p}`); // URLSearchParams stringifies itself

// Update the address bar without reloading
history.replaceState(null, '', `/search?${params}`);

// Built-in encoding — no manual encodeURIComponent needed
const q = new URLSearchParams({ term: 'hello world & more' });
console.log(q.toString()); // term=hello+world+%26+more
```
`URLSearchParams` parses `location.search` (or any `a=b&c=d` string) and safely encodes when building URLs — spaces become `+` and special characters are escaped automatically. Watch the difference between `get` (first value or `null`) and `getAll` (array), and between `set` (replace) and `append` (add another).

