```js
/* IntersectionObserver version — only when you need custom behavior,
   e.g. swapping data-src placeholders or adding a fade-in on load */
const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries, obs) => {
  entries.forEach(en => {
    if (!en.isIntersecting) return;
    const img = en.target;
    img.src = img.dataset.src;
    img.addEventListener('load', () => img.classList.add('loaded'), { once: true });
    obs.unobserve(img);
  });
}, { rootMargin: '200px 0px' });
document.querySelectorAll('img[data-src]').forEach(img => io.observe(img));
```

Why it works: loading='lazy' is now supported in all evergreen browsers and uses the browser's own viewport distance heuristics — it should be your default. The width and height attributes are essential: they let the browser reserve space before the image arrives, preventing layout shift (CLS). rootMargin 200px in the IO version starts the fetch slightly before the image scrolls into view, which hides the network latency. The rule of thumb: native lazy loading for everything below the fold, and eager + preload + fetchpriority=high for the LCP hero image — lazy-loading your largest visible image actively hurts your LCP score.

کرونومتر دقیق با محاسبه مبتنی بر timestamp (بدون خطای انباشته):

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang='fa' dir='rtl'>
<head>
<meta charset='UTF-8'>
<meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0'>
<title>کرونومتر</title>
<style>
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { min-height: 100vh; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; background: #111; }
  .box { text-align: center; }
  #display { color: #0f0; font-size: 56px; letter-spacing: 2px; direction: ltr; font-family: monospace; }
  .btns { margin-top: 24px; display: flex; gap: 12px; justify-content: center; }
  button { padding: 11px 26px; border: 0; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 15px; cursor: pointer; font-family: Tahoma; }
  #startBtn { background: #2e7d32; color: #fff; }
  #stopBtn { background: #e53935; color: #fff; }
  #resetBtn { background: #555; color: #fff; }
  button:disabled { opacity: .4; cursor: not-allowed; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class='box'>
    <div id='display'>00:00.00</div>
    <div class='btns'>
      <button id='startBtn'>شروع</button>
      <button id='stopBtn' disabled>توقف</button>
      <button id='resetBtn'>ریست</button>
    </div>
  </div>
<script>
  const display = document.querySelector('#display');
  const startBtn = document.querySelector('#startBtn');
  const stopBtn = document.querySelector('#stopBtn');
  const resetBtn = document.querySelector('#resetBtn');

  let startTime = 0;   // timestamp لحظه شروع
  let accumulated = 0; // زمان جمع‌شده قبل از آخرین توقف
  let rafId = null;

  function format(ms) {
    const m = Math.floor(ms / 60000);
    const s = Math.floor((ms % 60000) / 1000);
    const cs = Math.floor((ms % 1000) / 10);
    return `${String(m).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(s).padStart(2, '0')}.${String(cs).padStart(2, '0')}`;
  }

  function tick() {
    display.textContent = format(accumulated + (Date.now() - startTime));
    rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }

  startBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    startTime = Date.now();
    rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    startBtn.disabled = true;
    stopBtn.disabled = false;
  });

  stopBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    accumulated += Date.now() - startTime;
    cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);
    startBtn.disabled = false;
    stopBtn.disabled = true;
  });

  resetBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);
    accumulated = 0;
    display.textContent = '00:00.00';
    startBtn.disabled = false;
    stopBtn.disabled = true;
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

چرا این روش دقیق است؟
- به‌جای شمارش تیک‌ها (که خطا انباشته می‌کند) زمان از اختلاف `Date.now()` محاسبه می‌شود؛ حتی اگر تب مدتی فریز شود عدد درست می‌ماند.
- به‌جای setInterval از `requestAnimationFrame` استفاده شده که با نرخ رفرش مانیتور همگام است و پرش نمی‌زند.
- `padStart(2, '0')` اعداد را همیشه دورقمی نگه می‌دارد تا عرض نمایش ثابت بماند و ارقام نپرند.
- دکمه‌ها با disabled از اجرای همزمان دو state جلوگیری می‌کنند (مثلا دوبار زدن شروع).
- برای ادامه بعد از توقف، startTime دوباره ست می‌شود و زمان قبلی در accumulated جمع می‌شود — همان الگوی کرونومترهای واقعی.

**Grid page layouts — Beginner to Expert**

[Beginner]
Define the page as named rows: header, content, footer — and let main content flex.
```css
body { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto; min-height: 100vh; margin: 0; }
```
Why it works: the `1fr` middle row absorbs leftover height, pinning the footer to the bottom.

[Intermediate]
Add a sidebar with `grid-template-columns` and named areas for clarity.
```css
.page {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-areas: 'header header' 'side main' 'footer footer';
  grid-template-columns: minmax(200px, 260px) 1fr;
}
```
Why it works: areas describe the layout in one readable place; children claim slots by name.

[Advanced]
Collapse the sidebar on small screens by redefining the template instead of rewriting children.
```css
@media (max-width: 48rem) {
  .page { grid-template-areas: 'header' 'main' 'footer'; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .page > aside { display: none; }
}
```
Why it works: only the container changes; every child keeps its `grid-area` assignment.

[Expert]
Compose with `subgrid` so card internals align across the page grid.
```css
.cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
.card { display: grid; grid-template-rows: subgrid; grid-row: span 3; }
```
Why it works: rows inherit the parent track sizes, so titles and actions align perfectly across cards.

