document.getElementById('yearly').addEventListener('change', e => {
  const yearly = e.target.checked;
  document.querySelectorAll('.price').forEach(p => {
    p.firstChild.textContent = '$' + (yearly ? p.dataset.y : p.dataset.m);
    p.querySelector('small').textContent = yearly ? '/yr' : '/mo';
  });
});
```

Why it works: prices live in data attributes so the toggle just swaps text — no duplicated DOM — and firstChild targets the text node before the small element without wrapping it in a span.

